Now the linux foundation announces the call-for-paper to the
Japan Linux Symposium 2009 held in Oct 2009, Tokyo.

  http://events.linuxfoundation.org/events/japan-linux-symposium

In this year, the kernel summit is also supposed to be held prior
to the JLS2009. Do you have any plan to attend the kernel summit
or submit a paper?

I have a plan to propose a session for web-application security
powered by SELinux, and a BoF to discuss where the enhanced
security feature should go (as a man in Japan secure os users
group) with developers and end-users in same place.
(Needless to say, they have a possibility to be rejected. :D)

It is nice, if we can provide more sessions related to security.

